Subject: [PATCH 0018] Prism: keep brand favicon colors on Prism WebUI pages

Chromium "themifies" favicons of chrome:// pages when their K-mean color
lacks contrast against the tab strip: the bitmap is replaced by its alpha
silhouette in the theme color. Once the LogiBricks favicon got standard
favicon padding (transparent margins), its K-mean fell below the contrast
threshold and the tab icon collapsed into a flat gray rounded square.

Exclude chrome://prism-welcome and chrome://prism-onboarding from
themification: the two-tone tile (dark tile, ivory bricks, terracotta dot)
is designed to read on both light and dark tab strips as-is.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/favicon/favicon_utils.cc b/chrome/browser/favicon/favicon_utils.cc
index c674695868..dd2b919d7d 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/favicon/favicon_utils.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/favicon/favicon_utils.cc
@@ -184,6 +184,11 @@ bool ShouldThemifyFavicon(GURL url) {
   if (!url.SchemeIs(content::kChromeUIScheme)) {
     return false;
   }
+  // Prism: the brand favicons on our WebUI pages keep their real colors —
+  // the two-tone LogiBricks tile reads on light and dark tab strips as-is.
+  if (url.host() == "prism-welcome" || url.host() == "prism-onboarding") {
+    return false;
+  }
   return url.host() != chrome::kChromeUIAppLauncherPageHost &&
          url.host() != chrome::kChromeUIHelpHost &&
          url.host() != chrome::kChromeUIVersionHost &&
